        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 81.754,
          "end": 84.517,
          "en": "And in that file, scroll down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.517,
          "end": 89.517,
          "en": "until you find this commented out assets part here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.7,
          "end": 92.22,
          "en": "Now you can comment this in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.22,
          "end": 95.72999999999999,
          "en": "by simply removing these hash symbols here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "and you should make sure that you have one level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 100.56,
          "en": "of indentation here by hitting the tab key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 103.92,
          "en": "And then you add a list of all the assets, all the images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.92,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "for example, that should be available in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 109.77000000000001,
          "en": "Just adding these files in your project folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.77000000000001,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 114.33,
          "en": "If you want to be able to display these images in your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.33,
          "end": 116.043,
          "en": "you have to register them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "And for that you have to specify a relative path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 123.48,
          "en": "the relative path to the images that should be included.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.48,
          "end": 127.04,
          "en": "So in my case assets, since I have this assets folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.04,
          "end": 131.1,
          "en": "/images, since I have that images sub folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 134.61,
          "en": "and then the name of the images, dice-1.png,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 138.51,
          "en": "but then also dice-2, dice-3, dice-4, dice-5,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.51,
          "end": 140.28,
          "en": "and dice-6.png.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.28,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "All these image paths should be added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 146.703,
          "en": "to assets in your pubsec.yml file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.836,
          "end": 152.801,
          "en": "Now with that added, you can use those images in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.801,
          "end": 156.414,
          "en": "And here we could do this in gradient container instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.414,
          "end": 158.44,
          "en": "of this text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.44,
          "end": 162,
          "en": "because this text here is not needed right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162,
          "end": 164.76,
          "en": "Instead here I want to output one of these images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.76,
          "end": 166.65,
          "en": "and later we will add logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.65,
          "end": 169.19400000000002,
          "en": "to change this image dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.19400000000002,
          "end": 171,
          "en": "Now to output an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 171,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "we can use the built-in image widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 174.993,
          "en": "which is provided by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.98,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "You can create it like this to then set an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 182.49,
          "en": "but for that you need a so-called image provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.49,
          "end": 185.73,
          "en": "which is another object, which in the end resolves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 185.73,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "to a certain image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 191.13,
          "en": "This could be done, but if you have a locally stored image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.13,
          "end": 193.5,
          "en": "so such a asset which we just registered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 196.53,
          "en": "in a pubspec.yml file, there is a quicker way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 196.53,
          "end": 197.823,
          "en": "of referencing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 203.75,
          "en": "You can use Image. and then the asset constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.108,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "Now this is using a feature built into Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 210.655,
          "en": "where you can define multiple constructor functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 210.655,
          "end": 213.42000000000002,
          "en": "in a given class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.42000000000002,
          "end": 215.91,
          "en": "We could do this in our own classes as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 218.07,
          "en": "For example, here in GradientContainer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 218.07,
          "end": 220.92000000000002,
          "en": "we have this default constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 220.92000000000002,
          "end": 223.89,
          "en": "but we could also add a second constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 223.89,
          "end": 227.61,
          "en": "by again using our class name and then dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 227.61,
          "end": 230.73,
          "en": "and then the actual constructor function we want to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.73,
          "end": 235.65,
          "en": "For example, purple to then, for example, set color one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.65,
          "end": 240.6,
          "en": "to some hard-coded deep purple value like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.6,
          "end": 242.25,
          "en": "and then separated by a comma.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.25,
          "end": 244.71,
          "en": "You could and should also set color2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 244.71,
          "end": 249.603,
          "en": "to some predefined value like Colors.indigo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.25,
          "end": 253.71,
          "en": "Then you could add cons here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.71,
          "end": 257.28,
          "en": "and also accept that named key parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.28,
          "end": 261.12,
          "en": "And now you would have an alternative constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.12,
          "end": 265.02,
          "en": "that can be used whenever a gradient container is used so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 265.02,
          "end": 266.67,
          "en": "that instead of using it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.67,
          "end": 269.37,
          "en": "and passing those specific colors to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.37,
          "end": 271.95,
          "en": "you could use the purple constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.95,
          "end": 274.859,
          "en": "which here could act as a convenience constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.859,
          "end": 277.83,
          "en": "with some predefined colors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 280.29,
          "en": "And it's totally up to you what you would want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 280.29,
          "end": 283.86,
          "en": "to do in such additional constructor functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 283.86,
          "end": 286.54200000000003,
          "en": "Here, I'll go back to the previous usage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 286.54200000000003,
          "end": 288.65999999999997,
          "en": "but it is important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 288.65999999999997,
          "end": 291.212,
          "en": "that you can simply add multiple constructor functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 291.212,
          "end": 293.61,
          "en": "to the same class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 293.61,
          "end": 295.2,
          "en": "And that's in the end what we're using here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 295.2,
          "end": 296.97,
          "en": "with this asset function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.97,
          "end": 300.641,
          "en": "Image has a default constructor function used like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 300.641,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "and then multiple alternative constructor functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 306.809,
          "en": "which simply make adding an image a bit easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306.809,
          "end": 308.43,
          "en": "For example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 308.43,
          "end": 310.98,
          "en": "when using the asset constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 310.98,
          "end": 315.12,
          "en": "you pass a string to it, the name of the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 315.12,
          "end": 317.97,
          "en": "or to be precise, the path to the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 317.97,
          "end": 320.76,
          "en": "which in this case would be assets/image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 320.76,
          "end": 323.463,
          "en": "and then for example, dice-2.png.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 324.431,
          "end": 327.33,
          "en": "Now here, I then get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 327.33,
          "end": 330.3,
          "en": "because actually I should remove the const keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 330.3,
          "end": 333.69,
          "en": "because this image widget is in the end a dynamic widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.69,
          "end": 335.82,
          "en": "which isn't guaranteed to be const.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 335.82,
          "end": 339.54,
          "en": "So we must remove this cons keyword to avoid errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 339.54,
          "end": 341.627,
          "en": "But with that, we have this image here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.627,
          "end": 344.64,
          "en": "and since we now got rid of that styled text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 344.64,
          "end": 346.39,
          "en": "we can also get rid of this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 348.84000000000003,
          "en": "And if you now save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 348.84000000000003,
          "end": 350.97,
          "en": "and force a reload of the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 350.97,
          "end": 352.762,
          "en": "with this image added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 352.762,
          "end": 356.07,
          "en": "you should also see a image here on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 356.07,
          "end": 358.05,
          "en": "Though in my case, I got a typo here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 358.05,
          "end": 361.17,
          "en": "This should be assets/images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 361.17,
          "end": 364.35,
          "en": "The correct path of course, is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 364.35,
          "end": 367.14,
          "en": "And with that I now see my dice here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 367.14,
          "end": 368.25,
          "en": "Now it's a bit big",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 368.25,
          "end": 371.43,
          "en": "and thankfully the asset constructor function allows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 371.43,
          "end": 373.17,
          "en": "for additional configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 373.17,
          "end": 375.78,
          "en": "by adding another argument to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 375.78,
          "end": 378.21,
          "en": "In this case, the width argument, which you could,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 378.21,
          "end": 380.695,
          "en": "for example, set to 200 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
